.SS haskell\-nix.options.shell.exposePackagesVia
How the v2 shell\(cqs pre\-built library deps are made visible to tools
the user runs.
One of:
.IP \(bu 2
\(lqcabal\-store\(rq (default) \(em the composed store is copied into
\f[CR]\(ti/.cabal/store/<ghc>\-inplace/\f[R] via a shellHook (or the
explicit \f[CR]haskell\-nix\-cabal\-store\-sync\f[R] command).
\f[CR]cabal v2\-build\f[R] then reuses the units directly.
The shell\(cqs \f[CR]ghc\f[R] is left plain, so
\f[CR]runghc\f[R]/\f[CR]ghci\f[R] will not see the deps.
.IP \(bu 2
\(lqghc\-pkg\(rq \(em the shell\(cqs \f[CR]ghc\f[R] is wrapped with
GHC_ENVIRONMENT pointing at the composed store\(cqs package.db, so
\f[CR]ghc\f[R]/\f[CR]ghci\f[R]/\f[CR]runghc\f[R]/\f[CR]ghc\-pkg\f[R] see
every dep directly.
No files are written outside the shell.
Only affects \f[CR]shellFor\f[R] under \f[CR]builderVersion = 2\f[R].
.PP
