.SS haskell\-nix.options.useLocalGhcLib
Expose the GHC compiler tree (configured\-src + generated, the
\f[CR]compiler/\f[R] subdir thereof) to the planner as a regular
reinstallable package source.
Use this when the project depends on / constrains the \f[CR]ghc\f[R]
package \(em e.g.
\f[CR]ghc\-lib\-reinstallable\f[R].
.PP
The project\-level wiring differs by builder:
.IP \(bu 2
Cabal projects (see \f[CR]modules/cabal\-project.nix\f[R]) inject a
\f[CR]source\-repository\-package\f[R] block into
\f[CR]cabalProjectLocal\f[R] so cabal hashes the wrapped repo\(cqs
content into \f[CR]pkg\-src\-sha256\f[R].
Both plan\-to\-nix and the v2 slice see the same repo, so UnitIds align.
.IP \(bu 2
Stack projects (see \f[CR]modules/stack\-project.nix\f[R]) re\-add the
post\-plan \f[CR]packages.ghc.src\f[R] override that
\f[CR]modules/configuration\-nix.nix\f[R] used to apply unconditionally
\(em stack only supports the v1 builder for now, so the post\-plan
override is harmless (v1 doesn\(cqt enforce UnitId alignment).
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] boolean
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
false
.EE
.PP
